<!-- Keep the existing deep link and safety boundaries; the how-to is optional. -->
<section class="gr-access-guide" id="agent-access" aria-labelledby="agent-access-title">
  <div class="gar-v2-inner">
    <div class="gar-v2-eyebrow">WHAT WE CHECK</div>
    <h2 id="agent-access-title">Can an agent reach your business?</h2>
    <p>A website can work for people but block agents. Our free check reads one public page and its published bot rules. It cannot verify private Cloudflare settings or guarantee access for every crawler.</p>
    <p><strong>For Cloudflare sites:</strong> Business and Premium include an owner-assisted SAT review — Search, Agent and Training — at onboarding. The $500 Agent Ready profile purchase does not include a Cloudflare account audit or configuration work. <a href="/terms/#agent-access">Agent Access scope</a>.</p>
    <details>
      <summary>Cloudflare site? Open the access checklist</summary>
      <p>Search, Agent and Training (SAT) are separate policy choices. A public page loading does not verify these settings.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Sign in to Cloudflare and select the correct account and <strong>active domain</strong>. If your host or agency manages it, ask them to check. Repeat for each domain.</li>
        <li>Open <strong>Security → Settings → Configure AI bot policies → Configurations</strong>. Record Search, Agent and Training: Allow, Block on pages with ads, or Block on all pages. Choose intentionally, save, reopen and confirm.</li>
        <li>Check any remaining <strong>Block AI bots</strong> and mixed-purpose controls. Blocking Training can also block crawlers used for Search, including Googlebot, Applebot and Bingbot. Training is a separate owner choice, not a requirement for visibility; review that trade-off before changing it.</li>
        <li>In <strong>AI Crawl Control → Security</strong>, include inactive crawlers and inspect individual block switches. Ask your site manager to check conflicting rules. Keep WAF, DDoS protection, authentication and private areas protected.</li>
        <li>Check your public <strong>/robots.txt</strong>: it must be text, not your homepage. Reconcile named-bot rules, Content-Signal preferences, Cloudflare-managed robots and Bot Preference Sync. Re-fetch after changes and inspect real crawler traffic/errors; our checker is not a verified Googlebot or ChatGPT visit.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Cloudflare's September 15, 2026 defaults affect new domains and existing Free-plan zones with untouched settings. A current value alone does not prove whether a setting was inherited or deliberately chosen. Record the domain, date, values and who confirmed them.</p>
      <p>Dashboard labels checked September 15, 2026. Sources: <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/bots/additional-configurations/block-ai-bots/">Cloudflare AI bot policies</a>, <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/ai-crawl-control/configuration/ai-crawl-control-with-bots/">layered blocking rules</a>, <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/bots/additional-configurations/managed-robots-txt/">robots preferences</a>, and <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/press/press-releases/2026/cloudflare-allows-the-agentic-internet-to-flourish-with-a-simple-philosophy-your-content-your-rules/">September 15 defaults</a>.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

